{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And HaShem spoke to Moses, saying: Speak to the congregation, saying, Get you up from about the dwelling of Korah.</b> It never entered my mind to punish the entire congregation, for on the contrary, I know that they were not seduced by Korah. And what I said — 'Separate yourselves from the midst of the congregation' — I said concerning all Israel, that they should separate themselves from the company of Korah. And a proof for this is from what is said earlier: 'And HaShem spoke to Moses and to Aaron, saying' — what is 'saying'? To whom should they say this? Rather, HaShem wanted them to say to all Israel: 'Separate yourselves.' And Moses did not understand the words of HaShem, blessed be He, for the word 'saying' (לֵאמֹר) is the Torah's expression based on what follows at the end; but further down it says: 'Lift you up from the midst of the congregation' etc., for there it says: 'And it came to pass, when the congregation was assembled against Moses' etc. — for there they truly assembled against them; therefore He said to Moses and to Aaron: 'Lift you up' (הֵרֹמּוּ) — an expression of exaltation befitting Moses and Aaron according to their rank. But here He said: 'Separate yourselves' (הִבָּדְלוּ), for this He said to all Israel, since an expression of exaltation does not apply to the entire congregation, as stated. And Moses did not understand this from the difference of expression, for he had not yet heard the statement 'Lift you up.' And a proof for our words that 'הֵרֹמּוּ' is not an expression of separation: behold, it says afterward 'and he hastened to the congregation' — hear from this that they were not among them; so what is the meaning of 'הֵרֹמּוּ'? Rather, it is an expression of exaltation, for they all descended to Sheol, while you shall retain the greatness and the exaltation, for you shall become a mighty people, in order to fulfill the oath. And close to this interpretation the Ramban wrote in the name of R. H, and from there you may see what I added of my own to his words, for through them many difficulties are resolved."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:41:42.016816028Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}